Description: CVE-2026-32665 not applicable — DoQ/QUIC absent in unbound 1.17.1
 Documentation-only placeholder for Debian bookworm. DoQ was introduced in
 Unbound 1.22.0; bookworm ships 1.17.1 with no vulnerable code path.
Author: Root.io
Last-Update: 2026-08-07

--- /dev/null
+++ b/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE
+
+Summaries for scanner-reported CVEs where no code patch is required on Debian
+bookworm `unbound` 1.17.1.
+
+## CVE-2026-32665 — Not applicable on unbound 1.17.1 (Debian bookworm)
+
+### Overview
+
+CVE-2026-32665 is a remote DNS-over-QUIC (DoQ) denial of service in NLnet Labs
+Unbound: a `quic-size` budget bypass. The first two bidirectional streams on a
+new QUIC connection (stream_id 0 and 4) skipped the per-stream `quic-size`
+gate, so a client could force large buffer allocations from a short length
+prefix and exhaust DoQ capacity (CWE-770).
+
+- **Severity:** HIGH (CVSS 7.5)
+- **Vector:** CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H
+- **Requires:** Unbound built with `--with-libngtcp2` and `quic-port` configured
+
+**Upstream fix:** commit `01dfd2f4` in NLnetLabs/unbound, shipped in **1.25.2**.
+
+### Why bookworm does not need this patch
+
+| Item | Bookworm (1.17.1) | Affected releases |
+|------|-------------------|-------------------|
+| DoQ / QUIC subsystem | **Not present** | Introduced in Unbound **1.22.0** |
+| `doq_stream_*` / `doq_table_quic_size_available` | Absent | Present |
+| `ngtcp2` / `quic-port` listen path | Absent | Present |
+| Package version | `1.17.1-2+deb12u4` | Vulnerable where DoQ exists and is enabled |
+
+Debian 12 (bookworm) ships Unbound **1.17.1**, which **predates the entire
+DoQ/QUIC subsystem**. There is no vulnerable code path to backport into.
+
+Scanners may still flag this CVE because the Debian security tracker marks
+bookworm as open/vulnerable; that flag is overly broad for this target.
+
+### Verdict
+
+**No code patch required** — not applicable to unbound 1.17.1 on Debian
+bookworm. Treat scanner findings as a **false positive** / **not affected**.
+
+This `dummy.patch` only adds this documentation file for audit/compliance
+tracking. It does **not** change Unbound behavior.
+
+### References
+
+- Upstream fix: https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/commit/01dfd2f466d383370405d8ecf939570947f3523e
+- Advisory: https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/security/advisories/GHSA-v3cq-93xf-4p42
+- NVD: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-32665
+- Debian tracker: https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-32665
Description: CVE-2026-42944 - Heap overflow and crash with multiple nsid, cookie, padding EDNS options
 A remote attacker can craft a DNS query that contains multiple instances of
 the EDNS NSID, COOKIE, or PADDING options. When unbound encodes the reply,
 the per-option entries are accumulated in the outgoing EDNS option list
 without enforcing buffer bounds, which can lead to a heap buffer overflow
 or a crash.
 .
 This backport applies the upstream fix to the unbound 1.17.x series shipped
 in Debian bookworm:
   * util/data/msgencode.c: when serializing the outgoing EDNS option list
     in attach_edns_record_max_msg_sz(), check that there is enough room in
     the packet buffer for each option (header + opt_len) before writing,
     and only emit the trailing PADDING option when there is at least space
     for its 4-byte header.
   * util/data/msgparse.c: in parse_edns_options_from_query(), record
     whether NSID and PADDING options have already been processed for this
     query and ignore subsequent duplicates so that the response option
     list cannot be inflated by repeating these EDNS options. The COOKIE
     case from the upstream fix is intentionally omitted because the cookie
     handling code path does not exist in this branch.
 .
 The size_t signature changes for calc_edns_field_size / calc_ede_option_size
 and the extended_error_encode / ede_trim_text changes from the upstream
 commit are not applicable to this branch and have been omitted.
Origin: backport, https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/commit/fe946ba4e935a1528e6866e108e5bc9e7533ae18
Author: W.C.A. Wijngaards <wouter@nlnetlabs.nl>
Last-Update: 2026-06-03
