Description: Fix CVE-2026-50252 cache poisoning via per-thread source port pools
 Unbound allocated outgoing UDP source ports from a per-worker slice of the
 shared port population. Combined with SO_REUSEPORT worker pinning, an
 attacker who could observe or influence port allocation patterns could
 improve the odds of spoofing DNS responses (CWE-349).
 .
 Backport of upstream commit 804cff4c152a121961b04605f75132370fc80df4
 (unbound 1.25.2) to Debian bookworm's 1.17.1: introduce a mutex-protected
 shared_ports / shared_ports_if pool shared across threads, stop pre-slicing
 ports per worker, and adapt outside_network_create / worker_create /
 libworker callers. Upstream unit coverage in testcode/unittcpreuse.c is
 retained. Minor 1.17.1 adaptations: connect_sslctx naming (not
 connect_dot_sslctx) and no HAVE_NGTCP2/DoQ path in daemon_create_workers.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/commit/804cff4c152a121961b04605f75132370fc80df4
Bug: https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/security/advisories
