Description: CVE-2026-55973 not applicable — dns-error-reporting absent in unbound 1.17.1
 Documentation-only placeholder for Debian bookworm. RFC 9567 DNS Error
 Reporting was introduced upstream after 1.17.1; bookworm has no vulnerable
 code path.
Author: Root.io
Last-Update: 2026-08-13

--- /dev/null
+++ b/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE-CVE-2026-55973.md
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# CVE-2026-55973 — Not applicable on unbound 1.17.1 (Debian bookworm)
+
+### Overview
+
+CVE-2026-55973 is a stack buffer overflow in NLnet Labs Unbound's RFC 9567
+DNS Error Reporting feature (`dns-error-reporting`). A malformed agent domain
+name can overflow a stack buffer when `dns_error_reporting()` processes an
+EDNS Report-Channel (CWE-121 / related allocation/bounds issues).
+
+- **Severity:** HIGH (CVSS 7.5)
+- **Requires:** Unbound built with DNS Error Reporting support and
+  `dns-error-reporting: yes` configured
+
+**Upstream fix:** commit `96f87555` in NLnetLabs/unbound.
+
+### Why bookworm does not need this patch
+
+| Item | Bookworm (1.17.1) | Affected releases |
+|------|-------------------|-------------------|
+| DNS Error Reporting / RFC 9567 | **Not present** | Introduced upstream ~1.20.0+ (`dns_error_reporting()`, `REPORT_CHAN`) |
+| `dns_error_reporting()` in `services/mesh.c` | Absent | Present |
+| Package version | `1.17.1-2+deb12u4` | Vulnerable where the feature exists and is enabled |
+
+Debian 12 (bookworm) ships Unbound **1.17.1**, which **predates the entire
+dns-error-reporting subsystem**. Exhaustive search finds no
+`dns_error_reporting` / `REPORT_CHAN` code. There is no vulnerable path to
+backport into.
+
+Scanners may still flag this CVE from broad version ranges; for bookworm that
+is a **false positive**.
+
+### Verdict
+
+**No code patch required** — not applicable to unbound 1.17.1 on Debian
+bookworm. Treat as **false positive** / **not affected**.
+
+This `dummy.patch` only adds this documentation file for audit/compliance
+tracking. It does **not** change Unbound behavior.
+
+### References
+
+- Upstream fix: https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/commit/96f875552023c0ccf376ebe050519f12f3371dc9
+- NVD: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-55973
+- Debian tracker: https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-55973
Description: Fix CVE-2026-42960, possible cache poisoning while following delegation
 Unbound's iterator scrubber, when iter-scrub-promiscuous is enabled,
 accepts non-NS RRsets (e.g. MX) in the authority section of a referral
 and caches the accompanying address records from the additional section
 as glue. This allows an on-path or spoofing attacker to redirect
 subsequent name resolution to attacker-controlled servers.
 .
 The fix in scrub_normalize() (iterator/iter_scrub.c) guards
 mark_additional_rrset() so that only NS records in the authority
 section can mark address records as allowed glue. This is a complement
 fix to CVE-2025-11411.
 .
 This patch backports two upstream commits to Debian 12 (bookworm)
 unbound 1.17.1:
   * 8ae4b45 - the security fix in iterator/iter_scrub.c
   * 0d2282d - the regression test testdata/iter_scrub_mx.rpl
 .
 The doc/Changelog hunks from the upstream commits are intentionally
 omitted because the target Changelog is at the 1.17.1 release state,
 long before the fix entries were added.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/commit/8ae4b4545dccaaabd30b597b0dcb0d9640c8cc39
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/commit/0d2282d5513e73b526a44483d63fc5d0f9c41439
Bug: https://www.nlnetlabs.nl/downloads/unbound/CVE-2026-42960.txt
Author: W.C.A. Wijngaards <wouter@nlnetlabs.nl>
Last-Update: 2026-06-03

--- a/iterator/iter_scrub.c
+++ b/iterator/iter_scrub.c
@@ -566,7 +566,13 @@ scrub_normalize(sldns_buffer* pkt, struct msg_parse* msg,
 			rrset->rrset_all_next = NULL;
 			return 1;
 		}
-		mark_additional_rrset(pkt, msg, rrset);
+		/* Only mark glue as allowed for type NS in the authority
+		 * section. Other RR types do not get glue for them, it
+		 * is allowed from the answer section, but not authority
+		 * so that a message can not have address records cached
+		 * as a side effect to the query. */
+		if(rrset->type==LDNS_RR_TYPE_NS)
+			mark_additional_rrset(pkt, msg, rrset);
 		prev = rrset;
 		rrset = rrset->rrset_all_next;
 	}
--- /dev/null
+++ b/testdata/iter_scrub_mx.rpl
@@ -0,0 +1,191 @@
+; config options
+server:
+	target-fetch-policy: "0 0 0 0 0"
+	qname-minimisation: no
+	iter-scrub-promiscuous: yes
+
+stub-zone:
+	name: "."
+	stub-addr: 1.2.3.0 # ns.root
+CONFIG_END
+
+SCENARIO_BEGIN Test iterator with scrub of authority MX records
+; The test queries receive spoofed answers. The check queries see if
+; the record is returned by the original server or by a spoofed source.
+; The test domain is pollute3.mesa.
+; with ns.pollute3.mesa A records are tested for cache placement.
+; MX records and other records should not be allowed to make glue in cache,
+; when present in the authority section.
+
+; ns.root
+RANGE_BEGIN 0 400
+	ADDRESS 1.2.3.0
+ENTRY_BEGIN
+MATCH opcode qtype qname
+ADJUST copy_id
+REPLY QR AA NOERROR
+SECTION QUESTION
+. IN NS
+SECTION ANSWER
+. IN NS NS.ROOT.
+SECTION ADDITIONAL
+NS.ROOT. IN A 1.2.3.0
+ENTRY_END
+
+ENTRY_BEGIN
+MATCH opcode subdomain
+ADJUST copy_id copy_query
+REPLY QR NOERROR
+SECTION QUESTION
+mesa. IN NS
+SECTION AUTHORITY
+mesa. IN NS ns.mesa.
+SECTION ADDITIONAL
+ns.mesa. IN A 1.2.7.7
+ENTRY_END
+RANGE_END
+
+; ns.mesa
+RANGE_BEGIN 0 400
+	ADDRESS 1.2.7.7
+ENTRY_BEGIN
+MATCH opcode subdomain
+ADJUST copy_id copy_query
+REPLY QR NOERROR
+SECTION QUESTION
+pollute3.mesa. IN NS
+SECTION AUTHORITY
+pollute3.mesa. IN NS ns.pollute3.mesa.
+SECTION ADDITIONAL
+ns.pollute3.mesa. IN A 1.2.4.3
+ENTRY_END
+
+ENTRY_BEGIN
+MATCH opcode subdomain
+ADJUST copy_id copy_query
+REPLY QR NOERROR
+SECTION QUESTION
+attacker.mesa. IN NS
+SECTION AUTHORITY
+attacker.mesa. IN NS ns.attacker.mesa.
+SECTION ADDITIONAL
+ns.attacker.mesa. IN A 5.6.7.8
+ENTRY_END
+RANGE_END
+
+; ns.pollute3.mesa
+RANGE_BEGIN 0 400
+	ADDRESS 1.2.4.3
+
+; This is the spoofed answer that is returned.
+ENTRY_BEGIN
+MATCH opcode qtype qname
+ADJUST copy_id
+REPLY QR AA NOERROR
+SECTION QUESTION
+test3.atkr.pollute3.mesa. IN A
+SECTION ANSWER
+test3.atkr.pollute3.mesa. 86400 IN A 1.2.3.4
+SECTION AUTHORITY
+test3.atkr.pollute3.mesa. 86400 IN MX 20 ns.pollute3.mesa.
+SECTION ADDITIONAL
+ns.pollute3.mesa. 86400 IN A 5.6.7.8
+ENTRY_END
+
+; correct answer for the check query.
+ENTRY_BEGIN
+MATCH opcode qtype qname
+ADJUST copy_id
+REPLY QR AA NOERROR
+SECTION QUESTION
+check.pollute3.mesa. IN A
+SECTION ANSWER
+check.pollute3.mesa. IN A 1.8.9.3
+ENTRY_END
+RANGE_END
+
+; ns.attacker.mesa
+RANGE_BEGIN 0 400
+	ADDRESS 5.6.7.8
+
+ENTRY_BEGIN
+MATCH opcode qtype qname
+ADJUST copy_id
+REPLY QR AA NOERROR
+SECTION QUESTION
+ns.attacker.mesa. IN A
+SECTION ANSWER
+ns.attacker.mesa. 86400 IN A 5.6.7.8
+ENTRY_END
+
+ENTRY_BEGIN
+MATCH opcode qtype qname
+ADJUST copy_id
+REPLY QR AA NOERROR
+SECTION QUESTION
+ns.attacker.mesa. IN AAAA
+SECTION AUTHORITY
+attacker.mesa. 3600 IN SOA ns.attacker.mesa. root.attacker.mesa. 4 7200 3600 604800 3600
+ENTRY_END
+
+ENTRY_BEGIN
+MATCH opcode qtype qname
+ADJUST copy_id
+REPLY QR AA NOERROR
+SECTION QUESTION
+ns.attacker.mesa. IN A
+SECTION ANSWER
+ns.attacker.mesa. 86400 IN A 5.6.7.8
+ENTRY_END
+
+ENTRY_BEGIN
+MATCH opcode qtype qname
+ADJUST copy_id
+REPLY QR AA NOERROR
+SECTION QUESTION
+check.pollute3.mesa. IN A
+SECTION ANSWER
+check.pollute3.mesa. 86400 IN A 5.6.7.9
+ENTRY_END
+RANGE_END
+
+; Test query with authority section MX glue.
+STEP 10 QUERY
+ENTRY_BEGIN
+REPLY RD
+SECTION QUESTION
+test3.atkr.pollute3.mesa. IN A
+ENTRY_END
+
+STEP 20 CHECK_ANSWER
+ENTRY_BEGIN
+MATCH all
+REPLY QR RD RA NOERROR
+SECTION QUESTION
+test3.atkr.pollute3.mesa. IN A
+SECTION ANSWER
+test3.atkr.pollute3.mesa. 86400 IN A 1.2.3.4
+ENTRY_END
+
+; Check the cache contents, for query with authority section MX glue.
+STEP 100 QUERY
+ENTRY_BEGIN
+REPLY RD
+SECTION QUESTION
+check.pollute3.mesa. IN A
+ENTRY_END
+
+STEP 110 CHECK_ANSWER
+ENTRY_BEGIN
+MATCH all
+REPLY QR RD RA NOERROR
+SECTION QUESTION
+check.pollute3.mesa. IN A
+SECTION ANSWER
+; good answer
+check.pollute3.mesa. IN A 1.8.9.3
+; bad answer
+;check.pollute3.mesa. IN A 5.6.7.9
+ENTRY_END
+
+SCENARIO_END
Description: CVE-2026-40691 - Fix packet of death for DNSCrypt over TCP.
 A malicious DNSCrypt query received over TCP could trigger a buffer
 overflow when unbound curved (encrypted) the reply. When the reply was
 built for a TCP connection the advertised udp_size was set to 65535 and
 the reply buffer capacity was not taken into account before adding the
 DNSCrypt reply header and padding, so dnscrypt_server_curve() could write
 past the end of the buffer.
