Description: CVE-2026-44690 - Cross-zone wildcard cache poisoning via RRSIG.labels manipulation
 An attacker able to inject responses could exploit a manipulated RRSIG
 label count to make Unbound cache a wildcard-expanded RRset under a
 canonical parent name outside the RRSIG signer's zone of authority,
 leading to cross-zone cache poisoning when aggressive NSEC is enabled.
 .
 The fix adds three layered defenses:
 .
  * In dnskey_verify_rrset_sig() (validator/val_sigcrypt.c), reject a
    signature whose label count is lower than the signer name's label
    count as DNSSEC bogus.
  * In rrset_cache_update_wildcard() (services/cache/rrset.c), verify the
    wildcard's canonical parent name falls within the authority of every
    RRSIG signer before inserting the synthesized wildcard RRset into the
    cache. The static helper rrsig_get_signer() in validator/val_utils.c
    is made non-static (declared in validator/val_utils.h) so the cache
    code can extract signer names.
  * In validate_positive_response() (validator/validator.c), postpone the
    aggressive-NSEC wildcard cache update until the positive wildcard
    proof has actually succeeded, so unproven wildcards are never cached.
